  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Fructose is a polyhydroxy ketone, It reacts with HCN to form a cyanohydrin which on hydrolysis forms a alpha hydroxy carboxylic group.</p><p>Fructose on reaction&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaBH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;forms&nbsp;D-sorbitol and D-mannitol( Mannitol and sorbitol are isomers,&nbsp;the only difference being the orientation of the hydroxyl group on carbon 2), which on reduction with HI&nbsp;in presence of red phosphorous form n-hexane.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/124c83d8-4582-49c9-be61-840a40cd64ad-15-08-2022.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 247px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
